[6.471641, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docs/PERMISSIONS.md\n"]
[6.471828, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docs/PERMISSIONS.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[6.47329, "o", "# docshare access policy\r\n\r\nOwner: platform security. This is the policy every docshare endpoint must follow. Endpoint details are in `API.md`.\r\n\r\n## 1. Who is asking\r\n- Every `/api/...` request must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (the token is `users.token`). A request with no\r\n  token or an unknown token gets `401`. Two endpoints need no login: `GET /api/health` and share links `GET /s/<token>`.\r\n- A user belongs to one or more organisations (rows in `memberships`) and has one role in each: `member` or\r\n  `org_admin`.\r\n- Support staff are users with `users.is_support = 1`. They belong to no organisation and have no home organisation.\r\n\r\n## 2. The active organisation\r\n- Every request acts in one organisation, the *active organisation*: the organisation named in the `X-Org-Id` header,\r\n"]
[6.473349, "o", "  or, when the header is absent, the user's home organisation (`users.home_org_id`).\r\n- A member or org_admin may only make active an organisation they belong to. If `X-Org-Id` names any other\r\n  organisation, or one that does not exist, the whole request is refused.\r\n- The caller's role is their role in the active organisation. Someone who is `member` in one organisation and\r\n  `org_admin` in another is an org_admin only while that second organisation is active.\r\n- Members and org_admins act only on folders and files of the active organisation. A file or folder of another\r\n  organisation is refused, even if the caller also belongs to that organisation: they switch first by sending that\r\n  organisation's id in `X-Org-Id`.\r\n"]
[6.473416, "o", "- Support may name any existing organisation in `X-Org-Id`; no membership is needed. For support this only chooses\r\n  what the list endpoints show. If support names an organisation that does not exist, the whole request is refused.\r\n  Without `X-Org-Id`, support's list endpoints answer `400`.\r\n\r\n## 3. What each role may do\r\n| Action | Endpoints | member | org_admin | support |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| read | `GET /api/files/<id>` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| download | `GET /api/files/<id>/download` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| thumb | `GET /api/files/<id>/thumb` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| list | `GET /api/files`, `GET /api/folders`, `GET /api/folders/<id>/files` | yes | yes | yes, the organisation it names |\r\n| export | `POST /api/export` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| rename | `PATCH /api/files/<id>` | yes | yes | no |\r\n| share | `POST /api/files/<id>/shares`, `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | yes | yes | no |\r\n| delete | `DELETE /api/files/<id>` | no | yes | no"]
[6.473476, "o", " |\r\n| support console | `GET /api/admin/orgs` | no | no | yes |\r\n| who am I | `GET /api/me` | yes | yes | yes |\r\n\r\n- For member and org_admin, \"yes\" means: on files and folders of the active organisation only (section 2).\r\n- For support, \"any organisation\" means: any file of any organisation, whatever the active organisation is.\r\n- A list shows exactly the folders or files of the active organisation, and nothing of any other organisation.\r\n\r\n## 4. Export\r\n`POST /api/export` returns several files in one response. It is allowed only if the caller may `read` every requested\r\nid under the rules above. If even one id is not readable (a file of another organisation, a deleted file, an unknown\r\nid), the whole request is refused and the response holds no file at all.\r\n\r\n## 5. Share links\r\n- Creating a link (`POST /api/files/<id>/shares`) and revoking it (`DELETE /api/shares/<token>`) are the `share`\r\n  action on the link's file.\r\n- Anyone who has the link can download the file with `GET /s/<token>`, without logging i"]
[6.473532, "o", "n, until the link is revoked\r\n  or the file is deleted. After that, or for an unknown token, the link answers `404`.\r\n\r\n## 6. Refusals\r\n- A refused request gets `403` or `404`; either is fine (404 avoids confirming that an id exists). The only other\r\n  refusal codes are `401` (section 1) and `400` (support listing without `X-Org-Id`, section 2).\r\n- A refusal holds no file data: no file contents and no name of a file the caller may not read. An error message may\r\n  repeat the id it was sent.\r\n- A refused request changes nothing: no file is renamed or deleted, no link is created or revoked.\r\n"]
[6.47368, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[6.473699, "o", "root@d4316b90-138a-4838-9145-a379053571f7:/app# "]
[9.671677, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/files.py\n"]
[9.671891, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/files.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.674604, "o", "\"\"\"File endpoints: list, metadata, download, rename, delete.\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, Response, abort, g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required, require_active_org\r\n"]
[9.674657, "o", "\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"files\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_file_or_404(file_id):\r\n    row = db.query_one(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS}, content FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n"]
[9.674711, "o", "        abort(404)\r\n    return row\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef list_files():\r\n    org_id = require_active_org()\r\n"]
[9.674749, "o", "    rows = db.query_all(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS} FROM files WHERE org_id = ? ORDER BY name\", (org_id,))\r\n    return jsonify(files=[db.file_json(r) for r in rows])\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef get_file(file_id):\r\n    return jsonify(db.file_json(get_file_or_404(file_id)))\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>/download\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef download(file_id):\r\n"]
[9.674793, "o", "    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    return file_response(row)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef file_response(row):\r\n    resp = Response(bytes(row[\"content\"]), mimetype=row[\"mime_type\"])\r\n    resp.headers[\"Content-Disposition\"] = f'attachment; filename=\"{row[\"name\"]}\"'\r\n    return resp\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.patch(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef rename(file_id):\r\n    if g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n"]
[9.674818, "o", "        abort(403)\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    body = request.get_json(silent=True) or {}\r\n    name = body.get(\"name\")\r\n    if not isinstance(name, str) or not (1 <= len(name) <= 200) or \"/\" in name:\r\n        abort(400, description=\"bad_name\")\r\n    db.execute(\"UPDATE files SET name = ? WHERE id = ?\", (name, row[\"id\"]))\r\n    return jsonify(db.file_json(get_file_or_404(row[\"id\"])))\r\n"]
[9.674999, "o", "\r\n\r\n@bp.delete(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef delete(file_id):\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    conn = db.get_db()\r\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM shares WHERE file_id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\r\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\r\n    conn.commit()\r\n    return \"\", 204\r\n"]
[9.675133, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[9.675197, "o", "root@d4316b90-138a-4838-9145-a379053571f7:/app# "]
[10.165943, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/share.py\n"]
[10.166419, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/share.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.168065, "o", "\"\"\"Share links: create, revoke, and the public download behind /s/<token>.\"\"\"\r\nimport secrets\r\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\r\n\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, g, jsonify\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required\r\nfrom .files import file_response\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"share\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef now_iso():\r\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\r\n"]
[10.168177, "o", "\r\n\r\n@bp.post(\"/api/files/<file_id>/shares\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef create_share(file_id):\r\n    if g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(403)\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(18)\r\n    created = now_iso()\r\n    db.execute(\"INSERT INTO shares (token, file_id, created_by, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\r\n               (token, row[\"id\"], g.identity.user_id, created))\r\n    return jsonify(token=token, url=f\"/s/{token}\", file_id=row[\"id\"], created_at=created), 201\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.delete(\"/api/shares/<token>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef revoke_share(token):\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT s.token, f.org_id FROM shares s JOIN files f ON f.id = s.file_id WHERE s.token = ?\",\r\n                       (token,))\r\n    if row is None or row[\"org_id\"] != g.identity.org_id or g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(404)\r\n"]
[10.168247, "o", "    db.execute(\"UPDATE shares SET revoked_at = ? WHERE token = ? AND revoked_at IS NULL\", (now_iso(), token))\r\n    return \"\", 204\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/s/<token>\")\r\ndef public_download(token):\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT f.id, f.name, f.mime_type, f.content FROM shares s JOIN files f ON f.id = s.file_id \"\r\n                       \"WHERE s.token = ? AND s.revoked_at IS NULL\", (token,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    return file_response(row)\r\n"]
[10.168485, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[10.168547, "o", "root@d4316b90-138a-4838-9145-a379053571f7:/app# "]
[10.667208, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/export.py\n"]
[10.667432, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/export.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.668802, "o", "\"\"\"Bulk export: several files in one JSON response (used by the \"Download selected\" button).\"\"\"\r\nimport base64\r\n\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"export\", __name__)\r\n\r\nMAX_IDS = 50\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.post(\"/api/export\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef export():\r\n    body = request.get_json(silent=True) or {}\r\n    ids = body.get(\"file_ids\")\r\n    if not isinstance(ids, list) or not (1 <= len(ids) <= MAX_IDS) or not all(isinstance(i, str) for i in ids):\r\n        abort(400, description=\"bad_file_ids\")\r\n    # A selection always comes from one folder view, so the first file tells us whose files these are.\r\n    first = db.query_one(\"SELECT org_id FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (ids[0],))\r\n    if first is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n"]
[10.668851, "o", "    if not g.identity.is_support and first[\"org_id\"] != g.identity.org_id:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    out = []\r\n    for file_id in ids:\r\n        row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, name, mime_type, size, content FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n        if row is None:\r\n            abort(404)\r\n        out.append({\"id\": row[\"id\"], \"name\": row[\"name\"], \"mime_type\": row[\"mime_type\"], \"size\": row[\"size\"],\r\n                    \"content_b64\": base64.b64encode(bytes(row[\"content\"])).decode(\"ascii\")})\r\n"]
[10.668895, "o", "    return jsonify(files=out)\r\n"]
[10.669088, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[10.669108, "o", "root@d4316b90-138a-4838-9145-a379053571f7:/app# "]
[11.164483, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/folders.py\n"]
[11.164697, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/folders.py\r\n"]
[11.164723, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.166185, "o", "\"\"\"Folder endpoints: the folders of the active organisation and their files.\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, jsonify\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required, require_active_org\r\n\r\n"]
[11.166257, "o", "bp = Blueprint(\"folders\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/folders\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef list_folders():\r\n    org_id = require_active_org()\r\n    rows = db.query_all(\"SELECT id, org_id, name FROM folders WHERE org_id = ? ORDER BY name\", (org_id,))\r\n    return jsonify(folders=[db.folder_json(r) for r in rows])\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/folders/<folder_id>/files\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef folder_files(folder_id):\r\n"]
[11.166286, "o", "    org_id = require_active_org()\r\n    folder = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, org_id, name FROM folders WHERE id = ? AND org_id = ?\", (folder_id, org_id))\r\n    if folder is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    rows = db.query_all(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS} FROM files WHERE folder_id = ? AND org_id = ? ORDER BY name\",\r\n                        (folder_id, org_id))\r\n    return jsonify(folder=db.folder_json(folder), files=[db.file_json(r) for r in rows])\r\n"]
[11.166503, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@d4316b90-138a-4838-9145-a379053571f7:/app# "]
[18.742139, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/auth.py\n"]
[18.742532, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/auth.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.744375, "o", "\"\"\"Who is calling: bearer token -> user, plus the active organisation for this request.\"\"\"\r\nimport functools\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\r\n\r\nfrom flask import g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom . import db\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass\r\nclass Identity:\r\n    user_id: str\r\n    email: str\r\n    name: str\r\n    is_support: bool\r\n"]
[18.744443, "o", "    org_id: str | None          # the active organisation for this request\r\n    role: str                   # \"member\", \"org_admin\" or \"support\"\r\n    memberships: dict = field(default_factory=dict)   # org_id -> role\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _bearer_token():\r\n    header = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\r\n    if not header.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\r\n        return None\r\n    return header[len(\"Bearer \"):].strip() or None\r\n\r\n"]
[18.744538, "o", "\r\ndef load_identity():\r\n    token = _bearer_token()\r\n    if token is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    user = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, email, name, home_org_id, is_support FROM users WHERE token = ?\", (token,))\r\n    if user is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    memberships = {r[\"org_id\"]: r[\"role\"] for r in\r\n                   db.query_all(\"SELECT org_id, role FROM memberships WHERE user_id = ?\", (user[\"id\"],))}\r\n    # The web client only offers organisations listed by /api/me, so the header names one of the user's orgs.\r\n    org_id = request.headers.get(\"X-Org-Id\") or user[\"home_org_id\"]\r\n    if user[\"is_support\"]:\r\n        role = \"support\"\r\n    else:\r\n        role = memberships.get(org_id, \"member\")\r\n    return Identity(user_id=user[\"id\"], email=user[\"email\"], name=user[\"name\"], is_support=bool(user[\"is_support\"]),\r\n                    org_id=org_id, role=role, memberships=memberships)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef login_required(view):\r\n    @functools.wraps(view)\r\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\r\n        ident = load_identity()\r\n"]
[18.74459, "o", "        if ident is None:\r\n            return jsonify(error=\"unauthorized\"), 401\r\n        g.identity = ident\r\n        return view(*args, **kwargs)\r\n    return wrapper\r\n\r\n\r\ndef require_active_org():\r\n    \"\"\"The active organisation id; support must name one with X-Org-Id before listing anything.\"\"\"\r\n    org_id = g.identity.org_id\r\n    if org_id is None:\r\n        from flask import abort\r\n        abort(400, description=\"x_org_id_required\")\r\n    return org_id\r\n"]
[18.744855, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[18.744941, "o", "root@d4316b90-138a-4838-9145-a379053571f7:/app# "]
[27.67193, "i", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: docshare/routes/files.py\n@@\n @bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>/download\")\n @login_required\n def download(file_id):\n-    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\n-    return file_response(row)\n+    # Enforce active organisation for non‑support users.\n+    # Support staff may download any file, so we only require the org check for members/org_admins.\n+    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\n+    if not g.identity.is_support:\n+        # Ensure the caller has an active organisation and that the file belongs to it.\n+        org_id = require_active_org()\n+        if row[\"org_id\"] != org_id:\n+            # Use 404 to avoid confirming existence of a file in another organisation.\n+            abort(404)\n+    return file_response(row)\n@@\n @bp.patch(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\n @login_required\n def rename(file_id):\n     if g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\n         abort(403)\n-    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\n+    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\n+    # Verify the file bel"]
[27.672032, "i", "ongs to the active organisation for members/org_admins.\n+    if not g.identity.is_support:\n+        org_id = require_active_org()\n+        if row[\"org_id\"] != org_id:\n+            abort(404)\n@@\n @bp.delete(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\n @login_required\n def delete(file_id):\n-    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\n+    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\n+    # Only allow deletion of files within the active organisation.\n+    if not g.identity.is_support:\n+        org_id = require_active_org()\n+        if row[\"org_id\"] != org_id:\n+            abort(404)\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n"]
[27.672078, "o", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\r\n"]
